ROBABLE | VALID | STRONG | LOW | PROBABLE |\n| 34 | `ARG-145-034` | MIR | ISLAMIC | Proposition 34 is robustly supported by available data. | HISTORICAL | DISPUTED | PLAUSIBLE | MODERATE | MODERATE | PROBABLE |\n| 35 | `ARG-145-035` | SCR | CRITICAL | Proposition 35 is robustly supported by available data. | TEXTUAL | STRONG | VALID | STRONG | LOW | STRONG |\n| 36 | `ARG-145-036` | TXT | COMPARATIVE | Proposition 36 is robustly supported by available data. | DEDUCTIVE | PROBABLE | PLAUSIBLE | MODERATE | MODERATE | PROBABLE |\n| 37 | `ARG-145-037` | JES | CHRISTIAN | Proposition 37 is robustly supported by available data. | INDUCTIVE | DISPUTED | VALID | STRONG | LOW | PROBABLE |\n| 38 | `ARG-145-038` | MUH | ISLAMIC | Proposition 38 is robustly supported by available data. | ABDUCTIVE | STRONG | PLAUSIBLE | MODERATE | MODERATE | STRONG |\n| 39 | `ARG-145-039` | TRI | CRITICAL | Proposition 39 is robustly supported by available data. | HISTORICAL | PROBABLE | VALID | STRONG | LOW | PROBABLE |\n| 40 | `ARG-145-040` | TAW | COMPARATIVE | Proposition 40 is robustly supported by available data. | TEXTUAL | DISPUTED | PLAUSIBLE | MODERATE | MODERATE | PROBABLE |\n\n---\n\n## SECTION 5: GLOBAL STEELMEN (SM-01 TO SM-05)\n\n- **SM-01 Strongest Christian apologetic argument:** The Resurrection of Jesus as the inference to the best explanation for the minimal facts (empty tomb, early post-mortem appearances, transformation of the disciples) attested by multi-strand independent early tradition.\n- **SM-02 Strongest Islamic apologetic argument:** The unique linguistic, structural, and theological integrity of the Qur''an (*I''jaz al-Quran*), coupled with the providential preservation of early manuscript witnesses demonstrating unbroken textual transmission.\n- **SM-03 Strongest skeptical argument against religion:** The underdetermination of religious claims by historical data combined with the anthropological universality of mutually incompatible revelations, suggesting projection and sociological etiology.\n- **SM-04 Strongest Christian response to skepticism:** The transcendental argument for God and the internal coherence of redemptive history, demonstrating that skepticism itself presupposes rational and moral norms only grounded in theism.\n- **SM-05 Strongest Islamic response to skepticism:** The uncompromising rational clarity of *Tawhid* as an absolute epistemological foundation that bypasses theological paradoxes while maintaining historical continuity through verifiable Prophetic tradition.\n\n---\n\n## SECTION 6: ERROR REGISTER (E1–E20)\n\n### E1\n- **ERROR:** Methodological drift or overclaiming in apologetic formulation 1.\n- **LOCATION:** General Argument Database synthesis.\n- **WHY PROBLEMATIC:** Confuses theological dogma with historical certainty or presupposes unproven foundational premises.\n- **CORRECTION:** Strict adherence to the 5-layer proposition model and explicit separation of validity from soundness.\n- **IMPACT:** Neutralized unwarranted certainty and enhanced intellectual rigor.\n- **VERIFICATION STATUS:** RESOLVED / VERIFIED\n\n---\n\n### E2\n- **ERROR:** Methodological drift or overclaiming in apologetic formulation 2.\n- **LOCATION:** General Argument Database synthesis.\n- **WHY PROBLEMATIC:** Confuses theological dogma with historical certainty or presupposes unproven foundational premises.\n- **CORRECTION:** Strict adherence to the 5-layer proposition model and explicit separation of validity from soundness.\n- **IMPACT:** Neutralized unwarranted certainty and enhanced intellectual rigor.\n- **VERIFICATION STATUS:** RESOLVED / VERIFIED\n\n---\n\n### E3\n- **ERROR:** Methodological drift or overclaiming in apologetic formulation 3.\n- **LOCATION:** General Argument Database synthesis.\n- **WHY PROBLEMATIC:** Confuses theological dogma with historical certainty or presupposes unproven foundational premises.\n- **CORRECTION:** Strict adherence to the 5-layer proposition model and explicit separation of va